d have been rewarding in its  own right or I could branch off that and  and try to build something from scratch  with a lot of other awesome people and  try to make a go of it and really try to  solve this problem and I just felt I  couldn't pass up opportunity and and and  you you join it with about seven or  eight months now time we're doing this  interview in in late February of 2012  and and you know is there anything  that's been surprising or just as you  expect it it's you know exactly as you  visualize it while you were about to  leave McKinsey or you're disappointing  what's kind of your your view of things  so far yeah anything could have to have  an amazing crystal ball or something you  know exactly what it would look like I  really didn't exactly know what I was  getting myself into it all but it's been  I fell I live my life it's been really  fun I I've been really happy to be here  I think some of the things that have  been surprising you've just been you  know that the scale of change and the  pace at which we're working I mean I  guess when I joined in July we'd worked  with one school district Los Altos and  we're still working with them but  instead of working with four teachers  they were working with like whole bunch  of teachers in the district about 40 of  them then we have all these other  schools we're working with as well  really that's probably 12,000 oh yeah  it's growing so fast and what's amazing  is like you know we're working really  closely with these schools and that's  great for it for those few schools and  that's what we're really seeing a lot of  the innovation but then every time we  discover something exciting at a school  or working with we can just throw it up  online and then all these other people  around the world can see it and use it  to you or will say oh wow you know it'd  be great if we had exercises on this  topic or features on our site on that  would help schools in these ways and we  can create them with the rest